From ezivot at u.washington.edu  Tue Jan  6 20:57:51 2004
From: ezivot at u.washington.edu (Eric Zivot)
Date: Tue, 06 Jan 2004 12:57:51 -0800
Subject: Re: aggregateSeries problem
In-Reply-To: <3FFB2353.22622.2DCE6FD@localhost>
References: <3FFB2353.22622.2DCE6FD@localhost>
Message-ID: <000b01c3d497$c0674750$927260cc@zivotd800>

Wolfgang

You are not using the function
aggregateSeries correctly. You should only be passing one time series (your
ts). Your aggregation positions should be specified using a timeDate object
giving the breakpoints. Alternatively, you can use the by and k.by optional
arguments to easily specify regular break points. For your example, you should
use

 

aggregateSeries(ts,FUN=sum,by=”seconds”,k.by=15)

 

This create a timeSeries with 15 second
sums of the data in ts. 

Hope this helps. ez

 

