Message-ID: <5.2.1.1.2.20040109142844.043c2d10@mailhost.blackmesacapital.com>

'if' is not intended to accept vectors in the condition.  When given
a vector, it uses only the first element to decide whether to execute the
if or else block, and prints a warning to that effect:

> if (c(F)) T else F

[1] F

> if (c(T)) T else F

[1] T

> if (c(T,T)) T else F

Warning: Condition has 2 elements: only the first used: if(c(T, T)) T
else F

[1] T

> if (c(T,F)) T else F

Warning: Condition has 2 elements: only the first used: if(c(T, F)) T
else F

