"'if' is not intended to accept vectors in the 
condition.  When given a vector, it uses only the first element to decide 
whether to execute the if or else block, and prints a warning to that 
effect."

According to 
everyone who responded, I had a choice of adding all() or any() to my if 
condition.  For what I am doing, any() was the most appropriate, 
e.g.

if ( any(abs(wsold[good] - wsnew[good] )) < wstol/10 ) 
