From luis.apiolaza at forestrytas.com.au  Wed Jan 14 03:29:10 2004
From: luis.apiolaza at forestrytas.com.au (Luis Apiolaza)
Date: Wed, 14 Jan 2004 13:29:10 +1000
Subject: Does levelplot work inside a function? Summary
Message-ID: <s005442f.054@ft-gateway>

Thanks to Tim Hesterberg (Insightful) and Nick Ellis (CSIRO Marine) who quickly 
pointed out that You have to print(levelplot(...))
explicitly. levelplot is a trellis function; these don't actually plot 
anything, but return an object; printing that object actually creates
the plot.  Outside of a function the "printing" happens automatically, but 
inside the function you have to do it explicitly.

Cheers,

Luis

