Hi all,

For my money, switching workspaces / projects is a tricky business.
Have you tried separating your S+ sessions out?  In Windows .....

* Create a new directory called (say) "C:\Project"
* Create a shortcut to "S_HOME\cmd\splus.exe" in this directory (usually
drag and drop)
* Right click your new shortcut and add the line S_PROJ="C:\Project" to
the end of the target line (so the target line should now read something
like 'C:\Program Files\Insightful\splus62\cmd\splus.exe
S_PROJ="C:\Project"'
* Open S+ using this shortcut - click ok at the warning message
* Now your project directory is C:\Project
* Use the /MULTIPLEINSTANCES flag (see Programmers Guide) for multiple
S-PLUS sessions ...

This is tricky first time around, but it separates projects very neatly.
For example, in my C:\Project directory I can store all the
data/reporting files that go along with this project, keeping all my
pieces of work separate ...

I find this way of working very neat - I'm sure others will have similar
preferred methods of working .....

Hope this helps,
